#: ../../../projections/azim/azim_general_perspective.rst:22
msgid "Perspective projection"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../projections/azim/azim_general_perspective.rst:24
msgid ""
"The perspective projection imitates the view of the Earth from a finite "
"point in space. In a full view of the earth one third of its surface area "
"can be seen."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../projections/azim/azim_general_perspective.rst:28
msgid ""
"**g**\\ *lon0/lat0*\\ */scale*\\ [**+a**\\ *azimuth*] [**+t**\\ *tilt*]\\ "
"[**+v**\\ *vwidth/vheight*]\\ [**+w**\\ *twist*] [**+z**\\ *altitude*] or "
"**G**\\ *lon0/lat0*\\ */width* [**+a**\\ *azimuth*]\\ [**+t**\\ *tilt*]\\ "
"[**+v**\\ *vwidth/vheight*] [**+w**\\ *twist*]\\ [**+z**\\ *altitude*]"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../projections/azim/azim_general_perspective.rst:34
msgid ""
"The projection type is set with **g** or **G**. *lon0/lat0* specifies the "
"projection center and *scale* or *width* determine the size of the figure. "
"With **+a**\\ *azimuth* the direction (in degrees) in which you are looking "
"is specified, measured clockwise from north. **+t**\\ *tilt* is given in "
"degrees and is the viewing angle relative to zenith. A tilt of 0° is looking "
"straight down, 60° is looking 30° above horizon. The viewport angle in "
"degrees is described via **+v**\\ *vwidth/vheight* and **+w**\\ *twist* is "
"the clockwise rotation of the image (in degrees). **+z**\\ *altitude* sets "
"the height in km of the viewpoint above local sea level (If altitude is less "
"than 10, then it is the distance from the center of the earth to the "
"viewpoint in earth radii)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../projections/azim/azim_general_perspective.rst:45
msgid ""
"The example shows the coast of Northern Europe viewed from 250 km above sea "
"level looking 30° from north at a tilt of 45°. The height and width of the "
"viewing angle is both 60°, which imitates viewing with naked eye."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../projections/azim/azim_general_perspective.rst:51
msgid ""
"import pygmt\n"
"from pygmt.params import Axis\n"
"\n"
"fig = pygmt.Figure()\n"
"fig.coast(\n"
"    region=\"g\",\n"
"    projection=\"G4/52/12c+a30+t45+v60/60+w0+z250\",\n"
"    frame=Axis(annot=True, tick=True, grid=True),\n"
"    land=\"khaki\",\n"
"    water=\"white\",\n"
")\n"
"fig.show()"
msgstr ""

